6	# Coroutines Patterns
7	
8	Structured concurrency for Kotlin.
9	
10	## Coroutine Scopes
11	
12	```kotlin
13	// ✅ ViewModel scope (auto-cancelled)
14	class HomeViewModel : ViewModel() {
15	    fun loadData() {
16	        viewModelScope.launch {
17	            // Cancelled when ViewModel cleared
18	        }
19	    }
20	}
21	
22	// ✅ Lifecycle scope
23	class MainActivity : AppCompatActivity() {
24	    override fun onCreate(savedInstanceState: Bundle?) {
25	        super.onCreate(savedInstanceState)
26	        lifecycleScope.launch {
27	            // Cancelled when lifecycle destroyed
28	        }
29	    }
30	}
31	
32	// ❌ AVOID: GlobalScope
33	GlobalScope.launch { }  // Never cancelled, memory leaks
34	```
35	
36	## Dispatchers
37	
38	```kotlin
39	// Main - UI operations
40	withContext(Dispatchers.Main) {
41	    textView.text = "Updated"
42	}
43	
44	// IO - Network, disk
45	withContext(Dispatchers.IO) {
46	    api.fetchData()
47	    database.query()
48	}
49	
50	// Default - CPU intensive
51	withContext(Dispatchers.Default) {
52	    list.sortedBy { it.score }
53	}
54	```
55	
56	## Flow Patterns
57	
58	```kotlin
59	// StateFlow for UI state
60	private val _state = MutableStateFlow(HomeState())
61	val state: StateFlow<HomeState> = _state.asStateFlow()
62	
63	// SharedFlow for events
64	private val _events = MutableSharedFlow<Event>()
65	val events: SharedFlow<Event> = _events.asSharedFlow()
66	
67	// Collect with lifecycle
68	@Composable
69	fun HomeScreen(viewModel: HomeViewModel) {
70	    val state by viewModel.state.collectAsStateWithLifecycle()
71	}
72	```
73	
74	## Flow Operators
75	
76	```kotlin
77	flow
78	    .filter { it.isActive }
79	    .map { transform(it) }
80	    .distinctUntilChanged()
81	    .debounce(300)
82	    .catch { emit(fallback) }
83	    .collect { process(it) }
84	```
85	
86	## Error Handling
87	
88	```kotlin
89	// Try-catch in coroutine
90	viewModelScope.launch {
91	    try {
92	        val result = repository.fetchData()
93	        _state.value = Success(result)
94	    } catch (e: Exception) {
95	        _state.value = Error(e.message)
96	    }
97	}
98	
99	// supervisorScope - siblings don't cancel
100	supervisorScope {
101	    launch { task1() }  // Failure doesn't cancel task2
102	    launch { task2() }
103	}
104	```
105	
106	## Cancellation
107	
108	```kotlin
109	// Cooperative cancellation
110	suspend fun processItems(items: List<Item>) {
111	    items.forEach { item ->
112	        ensureActive()  // Check cancellation
113	        process(item)
114	    }
115	}
116	
117	// CancellationException handling
118	try {
119	    coroutineWork()
120	} catch (e: CancellationException) {
121	    throw e  // Don't swallow!
122	} catch (e: Exception) {
123	    handleError(e)
124	}
125	```
126	
127	---
128	
129	**Remember**: Structured concurrency = lifecycle-bound, cancellable, debuggable.
