427	## Best Practices
428	
429	### ✅ DO
430	
431	```kotlin
432	// ✅ Use platform dispatchers through abstraction
433	withContext(PlatformDispatchers.io) { ... }
434	
435	// ✅ Scope coroutines to lifecycle
436	scope.launch { ... }
437	
438	// ✅ Handle cancellation
439	try {
440	    longRunningTask()
441	} catch (e: CancellationException) {
442	    throw e  // Re-throw cancellation
443	}
444	
445	// ✅ Use Flow for state
446	val users: StateFlow<List<User>>
447	
448	// ✅ Provide meaningful coroutine names
449	scope.launch(Dispatchers.Default + CoroutineName("FetchUsers")) { ... }
450	```
451	
452	### ❌ DON'T
453	
454	```kotlin
455	// ❌ Don't use GlobalScope
456	GlobalScope.launch { ... }  // ❌
457	
458	// ❌ Don't block threads
459	runBlocking { ... }  // ❌ in production code
460	
461	// ❌ Don't swallow exceptions
462	launch {
463	    throw RuntimeException()
464	}  // ❌ unhandled
465	
466	// ❌ Don't use Dispatchers.Main directly
467	// Use PlatformDispatchers.main for KMP
468	```
469	
470	---
471	
472	**Remember**: Coroutines are your async foundation. Abstract platform differences, scope properly, and handle cancellation.
